{"event": "agent_result", "task": "single-agent", "role": "single_agent", "result": {"report": {"incident_id": "slack-user-043", "outcome": "probable_cause", "hypotheses": [{"description": "Cedar Slack user-token actions failed because the Slack auth configuration had the needed permission only under bot scopes, while the failing action required a user token and no user_scopes were configured.", "supporting_evidence": ["ev_0e985d9e82d6", "ev_c6d2d39be65a", "ev_315dcd1e5920"], "contradicting_evidence": [], "confidence": "high", "assumptions": ["The failing Cedar workflow uses the same Slack configuration shape shown in the observed request.", "The sandbox controlled comparison is representative of the production failure mechanism for this request type."]}, {"description": "A broader Slack provider outage caused the missing_scope failures.", "supporting_evidence": ["ev_5c76760e3107"], "contradicting_evidence": ["ev_0e985d9e82d6", "ev_ef8b2f66c4c8", "ev_315dcd1e5920"], "confidence": "low", "assumptions": ["This relies only on an incomplete historical analogy, not current-incident proof."]}, {"description": "An internal product regression or deployment around the incident caused the failure.", "supporting_evidence": ["ev_387a4b1218f7"], "contradicting_evidence": ["ev_387a4b1218f7", "ev_0e985d9e82d6", "ev_315dcd1e5920"], "confidence": "low", "assumptions": ["The observed deployment list is incomplete across all services, so absence of a relevant deploy is not proven; however the only observed deploy is unrelated and the controlled comparison points to configuration instead."]}], "recommended_actions": ["Configure the required Slack permission under user_scopes, not only bot scopes.", "Reconnect the intended Slack user connection after updating scopes so the user token is granted the required scope.", "Retest the failing user-token workflow and monitor Cedar failure rate/queue depth for recovery.", "If any workflows only need bot-token operations, keep them separated from